{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let no man or woman make further craftsmanship</b> — financial contributions are called מְלָאכָה, as in \"if he has not sent his hand against his fellow's property (מְלֶאכֶת רֵעֵהוּ)\" (Exodus 22:7), \"for the pace of the property (הַמְּלָאכָה) that is before me\" (Genesis 33:14), \"and all property (הַמְּלָאכָה) is despised and melts away\" (I Samuel 15:9). The meaning is that they should not bring any more thing for the work of the sanctuary. But it says 'let them not make further craftsmanship' in order to include the women, so that they would no longer spin the goats' hair. And behold, even the act of bringing is called making, and he withheld everything from them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:03.010351469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}